# `--stats` of a native run: the latency in microseconds (native code counts
# no statements).
R0124 runtime run.stats-latency-native    stats: scheduling latency p50 {p50us} p99 {p99us} microseconds (native code counts no statements)
# A native run under `SISU_RT_ALLOCS` (stage 2, decision 217): the runtime's
# allocations of values still live when the program ends.
R0125 runtime run.live-allocations        allocations: {count} of the runtime's live at exit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- driver

D0001 cli     cli.cannot-read             cannot read `{path}`: {reason}
D0002 cli     cli.usage                   usage: sisu <command> [options] [<file>]\n\nWithout a file, a command works on the package of the current directory (`sisu.toml`).\n\ncommands:\n  run [<file>] [args...]  check and run a program (`--watch` swaps in each save, `--sir` runs a SIR file, `--monitor` checks ownership while it runs, `--defer-borrow` runs a program the ownership checker rejected under the monitor, `--contracts=off|preconditions|all` sets what it checks, `--record LOG` writes its capability log, `--stats` reports the scheduler's numbers, `--stats stack-depth` a histogram of the frame depths, `--stats shared` each `Shared` construction site, `--native` compiles it to an executable and runs that, `--native --from-sir` a file of serialised SIR)\n  check [<file>]         report diagnostics (`--format=ids` for the conformance form, `--explain` for the signatures with their contracts, `--diary LOG` appends them and what resolved the last check's to a JSONL log)\n  build [<file>]         check and lower a package, writing its lockfile (`--native` also compiles a program to an executable beside its source, named by the file's stem or the package, or at `--output PATH`; `--native --from-sir` compiles a file of serialised SIR)\n  test [<file>]          run the tests and transcripts under the ownership monitor (`--no-monitor` without it, `--jobs N`, `--filter TEXT`, `--tag T`, `--skip-tag T`, `--update` for snapshots and transcripts, `--replay TOKEN`, `--sim` with `--faults P`, `--std` for the standard library's doc examples)\n  bench [<file>]         run the benchmarks (`--iterations N`)\n  replay <log>           run a recorded program again against its capability log\n  fmt [<path>...]        format files in place (`--check` reports what would change)\n  repl [<file>|<dir>]    an interactive session, with a package loaded from its directory\n  ws <file>              run a worksheet, showing each statement's value (`--run` with the real `System`)\n  lsp                    the language server, over standard input and output\n  new <name>             create a package (`--lib` for a library)\n  sir [<file>]           print the serialised SIR\n  tokens <file>          print the token stream (`--trivia` includes trivia)\n  parse <file>           `--tree` prints the syntax tree, `--ast` the AST built from it, `--print` reprints the source, `--shape` prints what formatting keeps\n  explain <code>         describe a diagnostic code\n  explain-borrow <file>:<line>  show every borrow live on a line\n  audit --ownership <file>...  count the uses of `Shared`, `Weak`, `Cell`, `Arena`, `Key`, `.copy()` and `unsafe` in each file\n\n`run`, `check`, `build`, `test` and `bench` take `--locked`, which keeps `sisu.lock` as it is. `run` and `test` take `--schedule-seed N`, `--explore N` (N seeds), `--scheduler random|pct|exhaustive` and `--depth N`.
